      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Mary and Angus Hogg",
      "description": "Tarbolton Motte From The Bailey The 12th century Motte at Tarbolton was surrounded on 3 sides by a Bailey.  In this view, the sloping edge of the Motte is seen from the flat platform that was the Bailey.  The Motte was the site of a wooden house or tower, which would be the home of the local lord.  The Bailey was a surrounding base court containing the necessary services, such as stables, kitchens and workshops.  Tarbolton Bailey would have been protected by a timber fence, combined with the naturally steep slope on 3 sides.  (Source:  The Castles of South-West Scotland\", by Mike Salter)",
